+# dsh-side patches
+
+These patches are for the harness source tree, not for this package. They exist
+because a documented capability of `bench-workspace-ya` still needs a
+general-purpose harness change that official extension points do not provide.
+
+## `session-title-projection-flush.patch`
+
+**Capability:** a session title committed by a title provider survives a host
+restart, so a cold session list shows the real title instead of falling back to
+the workspace name.
+
+**Target:** `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` (`/tmp/dsh-migrate-bench/plugin/.dsh-migrate/harness`,
+commit `0a53fb5`).
+
+**Change:** `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection-cache` treats `session/title`
+as a mandatory checkpoint point in `installWritePath()`, exactly like
+`turn/end`, plus the README/JSDoc updates and a focused spec.
+
+**Why a harness change:** a title provider commits `session/title` *after* the
+main request's `turn/end`, and a hard restart never fires `session/disposed`.
+The cache's remaining triggers (count threshold, `writeIntervalMs`) can leave
+that tail unwritten, so the cold-list row has no `title` value and
+`displayTitleOf()` falls back to the workspace name. A plugin can force a
+checkpoint through the public `sessionProjectionCache.write(session)` seam
+(this package's `index.js` does, as its fallback), but only the cache's own
+write path makes the behavior durable for every consumer, including the
+official browser.
+
+**Apply to a harness checkout:**
+
+```sh
+git -C <harness-checkout> apply <this-directory>/session-title-projection-flush.patch
+```
+
+**Verification record (2026-10-12, applied uncommitted on the checkout above):**
+
+- `pnpm install --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile --config.package-import-method=hardlink --filter . --filter "@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection-cache..."`
+  (the provided checkout is sparse, so `patches/` and `vendor/` must be checked
+  out first: `git sparse-checkout disable`).
+- `pnpm vitest run packages/session/session-projection-cache/tests/cache.spec.ts`
+  → `18 passed`, including the new `writes a durable checkpoint at session/title
+  (mandatory point)`.
+- Negative control: reverse-applying only the `src/index.ts` hunk makes that new
+  test fail (`expected -1 to be 1`, the row still holds the creation cut) while
+  the other 17 pass.
+
+**Re-verification (2026-10-12, same checkout, same uncommitted state):**
+
+- `git apply --check` against the pristine `0a53fb5` blobs of the three touched
+  files: applies cleanly, and the three files it produces are byte-identical to
+  the checkout's working tree.
+- `node_modules/.bin/vitest run packages/session/session-projection-cache/tests/cache.spec.ts`
+  → `18 passed` again.
+- Mount check: an isolated `$DSH_HOME` profile whose `dsh.profile.bundles` starts
+  with this package was booted with the installed `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` artifact
+  (`--dump-config` composed 146 entries with this bundle's row first and the
+  official `ui-workspace` row still enabled; `dsh web` then served on an
+  isolated port). An instrumented copy of `index.js` proved `apply()` runs in
+  the real host and that `ctx.get('sessionProjectionCache')` is resolvable at
+  flush time (undefined during `apply`, `write` present once activation
+  settles) — the fallback is wired, not silently dead.
+- The plugin's host half was exercised against a fake cordis Context (7 checks:
+  one debounced write per title burst, non-title events ignored, per-session
+  coalescing, warn-and-continue on a throwing write, silent degrade without the
+  service, disposer cleanup, lazy service resolution).
+
+**Upstream status:** no issue or pull request covers this exact change. The
+related reports are discussion
+[#5576](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5576)
+(a maintainer-confirmed cold-list title gap whose suggested direction is this
+patch), the seeded-session siblings
+[#5843](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5843) /
+[#5857](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5857), and
+the adjacent sidebar-seam request
+[#4879](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/4879)
+(this package's retired browser takeover now rides the shipped official seat, so
+no patch follows from it).
+External pull requests are disabled on the harness repository, so the patch is
+kept here. See `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/session-title-projection-flush/report.md`.
